// Caption.schema — the wstring(N) TABLE unit (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §3, kind 33).
//
// Its own file beside WideText.schema, in the same package, because the two
// halves of the row are two wires: WideText.schema is the packet wire's
// proving ground (SPEC.md §4.12) and this is the id-table wire's. The unit
// stays out of examples/ for the reason that one does — examples/ pins gate 1
// for all nine targets and eight of them refuse wide text on either wire.
//
// Every KIND 33 SITE the wire has is declared once here, and nowhere else in
// the file, so a gate that names a site names one declaration: a TABLE's own
// field, a `type` body's field the table reaches, a UNION ARM, and an ELEMENT,
// which is a type inside an array. `wstring(N)` as a MAP KEY has no site: it
// is refused by name, because a map's entries ride in `memcmp` order and
// little-endian code units have none (§2.8).

package wide

// The bounds are the packet corpus's, so the two halves of the row read
// against the same numbers: 7 is the corpus's buffer_size 8 and 4 its
// buffer_size 5. A bound of 4 is what makes a clamp expressible — five code
// units on the wire, four kept — and what puts a surrogate pair astride the
// cut when the fifth unit is a pair's low half.

// A `type` a table reaches, which is a closure edge kind 33 carries: its wide
// text is the packet emitter's storage read by the table wire's codec.
type Line
{
    text wstring(4)
}

// An arm is a field line (§2.6), so wide text is an admissible arm payload and
// rides under kind 33 with the arm's `L` as its BYTE length. The narrow arm
// beside it is what makes a respelling between the two an ordinary kind
// mismatch rather than UTF-8 bytes read as code units.
union Body
{
    wide   wstring(4)
    narrow string(4)
    count  int32
}

// The root: every site at once, so one instance exercises them all.
table Caption
{
    title wstring(7)
    line  Line
    lines [..3]Line
    body  Body
}

// A FIXED table (§2.2): no pointer in its by-value closure, so it takes the
// block form and its cook is one region of one node. Wide text's cooked
// storage is char16_t[N + 1] and an int32 used length in CODE UNITS (§7.2),
// and a fixed root is where that layout is asserted rather than derived.
table Stamp
{
    label wstring(4)
    seq   uint32
}
